<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Margaritus of Brindisi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1197</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Margaritus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brindisi">Brindisi</a> was an admiral of the Norman Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. Commanding the fleet of William II, he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia">Cephalonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakynthos">Zakynthos</a> and other Ionian islands from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> in 1185 and became their first count palatine. After the fall of the Hauteville dynasty he was arrested by Emperor Henry VI in 1194 and died in captivity in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/margaritus-of-brindisi.jpg" alt="Margaritus of Brindisi" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FocalPoint for this adaptation Original map : de:Captain BloodTranslation : Eric Gaba (Sting) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Normans_possessions_12century-fr_Margaritus_of_Brindisi.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
